      "skos:prefLabel": "IBM Turnaround",
      "skos:definition": "The recovery of IBM after record losses in 1992–1993, led by outside CEO Louis V. Gerstner Jr. (1993–2002), who cut costs, kept the company integrated rather than breaking it up, attacked an insular culture and refocused IBM on services, software and systems integration.",
