      "@id": "kt:mece-principle",
      "@type": "kto:Framework",
      "skos:prefLabel": "MECE Principle",
      "skos:definition": "A grouping rule from management consulting requiring that the parts of any breakdown do not overlap (mutually exclusive) and together cover the whole (collectively exhaustive), used to structure problems, analyses and arguments without double-counting or gaps.",
